When expanding a repository accordion, if there's a `uri` parameter in the URL, it will create duplicate `uri` parameters in the API call, which causes the wrong URI to be used for filtering.

The constructed URL becomes: `/v2/runs?uri=${accordion_uri}&uri_mode=exact&limit=0&uri=${url_param_uri}&...`

When FastAPI receives duplicate query parameters, it typically uses the last value, so the URL parameter's URI would override the accordion's URI, showing the wrong runs.

The fix is to pass `only_saved_filters=true` to `getFilterQueryStringFromURI()` so it skips the uri/filename/branch/machine filters from URL params and only includes `show_archived` and `show_other_users`:

```suggestion
            if(!$.fn.DataTable.isDataTable(table)) {
