**Do not mark failed reads as a valid sample.**

A failed `read_msr()` leaves the domain value at `0`, but `s.valid` is still set to `1`. The next delta for that domain then becomes “energy since boot”, which creates a huge fake spike. Fail the whole sample or track per-domain validity and skip only the affected outputs.  

